	(text "Sonar v1 - Digital sheet (T-011, D012): Cmod A7-35T DIP-48 socket, FT232H sync-FIFO header, generic PDM header, DNP RMII provision, TX control, test points."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6ffef3d5-6ae3-402d-8f23-cee40ba8deb9")
	)
	(text "AUTHORITATIVE PIN TABLE: orchestration/pinmap.md (generated by scripts/gen_digital_sheet.py).\nClock-capable pins: PDM_CLK_FB=pio40 (pkg W4, MRCC_34), FT_CLKOUT=pio47 (pkg U8, SRCC_34), ETH_REF_CLK=pio3 (pkg A16, MRCC_16).\nDIP positions + package pins VERIFIED 2026-08-26 against the live Digilent Cmod-A7-Master.xdc + reference manual fig. 8.1\n(reproducible: scripts/check_pinmap_vs_xdc.py)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 18.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "055df8b3-3b9d-4578-b653-98d1f6405b78")
	)
	(text "POWER STRATEGY (revised 2026-08-26; review-B1 fix): the DIP socket exposes exactly TWO power pins - pin 24 = VU (module\n5 V in/out) and pin 25 = GND (the ONLY module GND). There is NO 3V3 pin on the DIP. The carrier 5V rail (T-012 power tree,\nglobal net \"5V\") powers the module through R420 (0R 0603, populated by default) -> 5V_CMOD -> J40 pin 24. Backfeed\ncaveat: VU is the module's own USB 5 V in/out, so to program the Cmod from its own USB while the carrier is live, DNP\nR420 first (bring-up procedure in orchestration/rails.md). DIP pins 15/16 are XADC analog inputs via a 3.3V->1V divider\n(NOT usable for 3.3V digital): NC here. The FT232H breakout is self-powered from its own USB (its 5V pin is NC).\nBoard +3.3V rail source: T-012 power tree (not the legacy \"3.3V\" net)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 29 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d14514ff-ac27-4f39-9637-ec898b782c47")
	)
	(text "PDM HEADER CONTENTION RULE (D012): exactly ONE capture platform attached at a time - either the Cmod A7 in socket J40,\nor the Pico 2 (T-009) via ribbon on J42. NEVER both: both would drive PDM_CLK_SRC/PDM_CLK_EN into each other.\nMicrophones and the CDCLVC1112 clock buffer live on the array sheet (T-010/T-016); PDM_* nets cross sheets by global label."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 42.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "646adadd-02bb-4abe-ba0b-a5932785ac6e")
	)
	(text "TX control nets (TX_EN/TX_PH/TX_NSLEEP/TX_NFAULT/TX_PMODE) leave this sheet by global label to the TX h-bridge sheet (T-013).\nTX_NFAULT is open-drain: pull-up belongs on the TX sheet. Debug LEDs: use on-module Cmod LEDs (led0/led1/RGB) - see pinmap.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 52 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1df87687-6cef-4e04-b576-1d1861b00a86")
	)
